WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.735
♪ (TENSE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.969
SPEAKER:
<i> It was a rainy morning.</i>

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:06.239
We all went down
into our sanctuary space.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:10.043
I turned around, and there was
the man with the gun.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.078
OFFICER:
<i>Shots fired, shots fired!</i>

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.679
OFFICER 2:
<i>They have an active shooter
 in the building.</i>

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:15.548
MICHELE ROSENTHAL:
<i>We got a text that just said,</i>

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:18.218
"Active shooter
at Tree of Life Synagogue."

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.287
OFFICER 2:<i> Several persons
 barricaded inside.</i>

00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:22.888
NURSE:<i> Jerry and I looked
 at each other.</i>

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:24.256
<i>Jerry's a doctor, I'm a nurse,</i>

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:27.126
<i> and thought that somehow
 we could be helpful,</i>

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.596
so we moved in the direction
of the gunfire.

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:34.534 line:0%
OFFICER 2:

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.171
There's a great fear
among people that the culture

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:41.908
of White America
has been diminished.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:45.511
These groups are emboldened,
they're empowered,

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:46.479
and they're vocal.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.249
SPEAKER 2:
<i> The days when synagogues
just leave their doors open,</i>

00:00:50.849 --> 00:00:52.652
<i>I think those days are gone.</i>

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.455
SPEAKER 3:
<i> When you think about</i>

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:58.424
<i> what can come
of this sort of situation,</i>

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.893
<i> you need to think about
 the values for which</i>

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.429
the victims stood.

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:04.463
<i> ♪ Rest your head... ♪</i>

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.566
Whether Jewish, or Catholic,
or Muslim,

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:07.933
<i> everybody seemed touched</i>

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.201
because this could happen
to them.

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:12.671
<i> ♪ The earth might shake
 The winds may blow ♪</i>

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:14.874
Because of misconceptions
about both of our communities,

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:17.410
<i>a lot of people were surprised
to see the Muslim community</i>

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.912
<i> step up and help
 the Jewish community.</i>

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.314
Our religions are very similar.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.581
Our values are similar.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:27.620
<i> ♪ To raise a candle
 In their names ♪</i>

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:31.391
Parkland has been here.
The church in Charleston,
they were here.

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:33.759
ROSENTHAL:
<i> When there's a shooting,
 we text each other,</i>

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:36.262
'cause you'll just know
what each other's feeling.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:39.131
SPEAKER 3:
<i>It's about how we can change</i>

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.601
<i> other people's lives
 in a positive manner</i>

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.170
<i> because that is what
the victims would've wanted.</i>

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.874
SPEAKER 4:
<i>Their memories really are
a blessing for all of us...</i>

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.744
<i>and part of them continues
 to live on within us.</i>

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:56.215
<i> ♪ I'll hold you tight ♪</i>

00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:02.422 line:0%
<i>♪ Beneath the Tree of Life ♪</i>

